Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they may be used
• `event_date`: filter for the exact day ‘20201130’.  
• `event_name`: keep only purchase events (`'purchase'`).  
• `ecommerce.tax_value_in_usd`: numerator of the tax‑rate calculation.  
• `ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd`: denominator of the tax‑rate calculation.  
• `items.item_category`: dimension on which the tax‑rate is compared.  
• `ecommerce.transaction_id`: required in the final output.  
• `ecommerce.total_item_quantity`: required in the final output.  
• `ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd` / `ecommerce.purchase_revenue`: both shown in the final output.  

Typical filtering conditions  
• `event_date = '20201130'`  
• `event_name = 'purchase'`  
• `ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd > 0` (avoid division‑by‑zero)  

